From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: preserve AN7563 DSA TX channel mapping

The MediaTek DSA tagger records the destination switch port in both the
skb queue mapping and the special tag.  AN7563 has four QDMA channels but
only eight TX descriptor rings.  Its original transmit path selected the
physical ring by priority while retaining the DSA port as the descriptor
channel.

The unified path reduces the selected queue modulo the TX ring count
before transmit.  Deriving the channel from that reduced queue therefore
always selects channel zero on AN7563.  It also maps the default skb
priority to queue seven instead of the original queue zero.

Recover the AN7563 DSA channel from the parsed MediaTek tag and retain its
zero-based priority mapping.  Leave other SoCs unchanged.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -7040,9 +7040,10 @@ static u16 airoha_dev_select_queue(struct
 	 * index, rely on port id otherwise. Select QoS queue based on skb
 	 * priority.
 	 */
-	if (airoha_is(dev->eth, airoha_an7563) &&
-	    port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX) {
-		channel = 0;
+	if (airoha_is(dev->eth, airoha_an7563)) {
+		channel = port->id == AIROHA_GDM2_IDX ? 0 :
+			  (netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) ?
+			   skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) : port->id);
 		queue = skb->priority % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES;
 	} else {
 		channel = netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) ?
@@ -7407,8 +7408,13 @@ static netdev_tx_t __airoha_dev_xmit(stru
 					     &skb_meta);
 		tag = skb_meta.mtk_tag;
 		chn = skb_meta.channel;
+		if (!airoha_is(qdma->eth, airoha_an7563) ||
+		    chn == AIROHA_MTK_INVALID_CHANNEL)
+			chn = qid / AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES;
+		else
+			chn %= AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS;
 		msg0 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_CHAN_MASK,
-				  qid / AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES) |
+				  chn) |
 		       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_QUEUE_MASK,
 				  qid % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_QUEUES) |
 		       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_SP_TAG_MASK, tag);
